# de_chunk_01 — Processing Summary

Total URLs processed: 50
Succeeded: 50
Failed: 0

## Method note

The first 22 pages were processed via the WebFetch tool. From URL #23 onward, WebFetch began
returning persistent HTTP 429 (Too Many Requests) — likely a shared rate limit on the fetch
backend, compounded by a concurrent sibling process also crawling dietz.eu in this same session
(evidenced by pre-existing files/assets for other URL chunks found in the project). Direct `curl`
requests to the same URLs returned clean 200s throughout, confirming the site itself was not
blocking us.

To keep the batch moving without long waits, switched to a direct pipeline for the remaining 29
pages: `curl` (with a browser User-Agent) + a small BeautifulSoup/lxml Python script
(`c01_extract.py` / `c01_gen_md.py`, scratchpad) that pulls page title, H1/H2/H3/H4 structure with
body copy in document order, images (absolute src + alt), YouTube/Vimeo iframe src, internal
dietz.eu links in the main content, and CTA text / form field names. This produced more complete
and verbatim page copy than the WebFetch summarization pass (no content loss from AI
condensation), so quality is equal or better for the back half of the batch.

## Failures

None. Every one of the 50 URLs resolved to a markdown file under `reference/pages/de/`.

## Images

- Unique image URLs found referenced across this chunk's 50 pages: 11
  - 10 certification/award badges on the `downloads/` page (DEKRA ISO 9001, DEKRA IATF 16949,
    ISO 14001:2015, EMAS 2020, Umweltpakt Bayern, DIHK/KSU, UMPreis 2023, UMPreis 2024, EcoVadis
    medal, AEO)
  - 1 staff photo (Andrea-Dietz.jpg) on the `elektroniker-m-w-d/` job posting page
- Downloaded this run: 0 (all 11 already existed in `reference/assets/images/{de,en}/` from
  earlier/concurrent crawling of overlapping shared assets — logos, badges, and the staff photo
  repeat across many pages/chunks). Verified each with `file` — all non-zero size, correct image
  type (PNG/JPEG).
- All other 48 pages in this chunk are text-only blog/glossary articles with no in-content images
  (confirmed both by the WebFetch passes and by the BeautifulSoup image scan, which only looks
  inside `<article> .post-content` — global header/footer/nav images are intentionally excluded
  per the task instructions and are already captured in `reference/nav-and-footer.md`).

## Content notes

- No embedded YouTube/Vimeo videos found on any of the 50 pages.
- Only two pages had real internal-content links or forms:
  - `elektroniker-m-w-d/` — a job-application form (fields: stelle, name, e-mail, telefon,
    bewerbungs-dateien[], text, ihr-nachricht) plus links to `/tag/ab-sofort/`, `/tag/vollzeit/`,
    and the relaunch site's Datenschutz page.
  - `downloads/` — ~30 outbound links to PDF documents (certificates, policies, brochures,
    sustainability reports) hosted under `wp-content/uploads/`.
  - A handful of the SEO blog articles link back to their related product category page (e.g.
    `druckfedern-nach-din-2095/` → `/produkte/druckfedern/`, `edelstahl-zugfedern/` →
    `/produkte/zugfedern/`, `doppelschenkelfedern-mechanische-systeme/` →
    `/produkte/schenkelfedern/`).
- Nearly every blog/glossary page carries the same repeated CTA text block:
  "Jetzt unverbindlich Kontakt mit uns aufnehmen" (not a distinct button/form, just styled text
  above the site-wide contact widget).
